  "body": "Follow-ups from the review of PR #823 (fixture plates), left out of that PR's review-fix push as non-blocking notes.\n\n1. **Rider geometry edits aren't re-checked.** Re-importing a rider (`ImportFixture` keeps its `mount`) or editing a vise rider's jaws (#802) changes its mesh without re-standing it on the plate top or re-running the overhang law. The recorded location stays, but the fixture may float, sink or hang off. Posting still judges the real meshes, so nothing gouges silently - but the label can lie. Fix: re-seat the rider in the same command (stand + on-the-plate law), or unmount it with a note when it no longer fits.\n2. **The dowel group can be any second lattice.** `detect` takes the next same-size group that forms a lattice as the dowels; four corner mounting holes of another size form a 2x2 lattice and become \"dowels\". Places are still real holes (only names are affected). Fix: a heuristic (dowel lattice inside the tapped grid's extent, a pitch that is a multiple of the grid pitch, or a minimum count), or ask the user.\n3. **File sizes.** Growth on files already over ~400 lines: `crates/ui/src/state.rs` (+33, ~4189), `crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell.rs` (+10), `crates/ui/src/egui_app/pages.rs` (+5); `crates/app/tests/fixture_plate.rs` sits at 402. Split along the plate seam where it helps.\n\nDone means: a rider whose geometry changes is re-seated or unmounted in the same undo step (pinned); the dowel pick has a rule that refuses a stray corner-hole set (pinned); the touched files are back under the 400-line law or have a split filed.\n\nPart of #819\n",
